+# Starred items
+
+**Go:** go, starred items stay in place in the full list (2026-10-12)
+
+## Intent
+
+The owner: "Let me star items and show only the starred ones." Starred items are the ones the
+owner wants to come back to; the starred view is a shorter list of just those.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Starred items keep their place in the full list: the owner wants the order unchanged; rejected:
+  sorting starred items to the top (owner, 2026-10-12)
+- The view is a query parameter (`/?show=starred`), so each view has its own link and the app stays
+  GET-only; rejected: a cookie that remembers the view (owner, 2026-10-12)
+
+## Acceptance items
+
+- **AC-1** A migration adds a starred flag to items, and every existing item starts unstarred.
+- **AC-2** In the list, every starred item shows ★ before its title, and unstarred items show no ★.
+- **AC-3** `/?show=starred` lists only the starred items, in the same order as the full list.
+- **AC-4** `/` and `/?show=all` list all items in id order, as before.
+- **AC-5** The page links to the other view: "Starred only" on the full list, "All items" on the
+  starred list.
+- **AC-6** Any other `show` value must answer 400 and list nothing.
+- **AC-7** `/?show=starred` is listed in `traffic/routes.json`, so synthetic traffic exercises it.
+
+## Core flow
+
+1. Open the list: every item, starred ones marked ★.
+2. Follow "Starred only": just the starred items.
+3. Follow "All items": back to the full list.
+
+## States
+
+| State            | List shows    | Message               | Link to      |
+| ---------------- | ------------- | --------------------- | ------------ |
+| Full list        | every item    | none                  | Starred only |
+| Empty table      | nothing       | No items yet.         | Starred only |
+| Starred view     | starred items | none                  | All items    |
+| No starred items | nothing       | No starred items yet. | All items    |
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Starring or unstarring from the page: there is no write route yet; items are starred in the
+  database.
+- Sorting or counting starred items.
